Maintainer: Albrecht Gebhardt <albrecht.gebhardt@aau.at>
Description: Provides an easy-to-use interface to OpenCL GPGPU 
    (General-Purpose Computing on Graphics Processing Units) 
    acceleration using a unified C++ abstraction layer via 'Rcpp'. 
    Enables developers to write, compile, and execute hardware-adaptive 
    inline OpenCL C kernels seamlessly from within the R environment. 
    Manages low-level memory transfer, device mapping, and execution 
    queues automatically. Configuration and cross-platform compilation 
    are handled via an integrated 'CMake' infrastructure. The core 
    architecture provides a Just-In-Time (JIT) compilation framework 
    with precision fallbacks and an efficient evaluation-in-place function 
    caching system to eliminate compile-on-invocation overheads.
